Mesh: bound a shared lightmap's texture index before it indexes the texture list.

`Mesh::load`'s LIGHTMAPS_SHARED (`0xB026`) branch reads a texture list sized by
one file-supplied count and then, per lightmap, a second file-supplied index
into it:

	std::uint32_t texture_index = c->read_uint();

	this->lightmaps.emplace_back(
	    LightMap {lightmap_textures[texture_index], {normal_a, normal_b}, origin});

`lightmap_textures` is a `std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Texture>>` and
`operator[]` is unchecked, so an out-of-range index does not merely read past
the allocation -- it copy-constructs a `shared_ptr` from whatever is there,
which increments a refcount through a wild control-block pointer and then
decrements it again when the world is freed.

Found by fuzzing `test/fixtures/minimal.g2.zen`: seed 39 of the run recorded in
`docs/plans/level-editor.md` 16.11 delta-debugs down to **one byte** -- file
offset 899, byte 2 of the third lightmap's texture index, turning a valid 0 into
3,932,160 against a list of three textures. The committed regression test seeds
the same defect by structure, rewriting the last four bytes of the 0xB026 chunk
(which are, by the chunk's layout, the last lightmap's texture index).

The fix is the same narrow shape as `0027`, `0029` and `0030`: compare the index
the file supplies against what it is actually allowed to address and throw a
named `ParserError`. This is one more instance of the unvalidated-count class in
16.11, not the class-level fix -- `_parse_bsp_nodes` still recurses once per
file-supplied flag bit with no depth bound, the chunk-walking loops elsewhere in
this same file are untouched, and the general fix (making `ReadMemory::seek`
clamp or throw) is still deferred.

Upstreamable as-is: a plain bounds-check bug, no API change, one guard.

diff --git a/src/Mesh.cc b/src/Mesh.cc
--- a/src/Mesh.cc
+++ b/src/Mesh.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 #include "zenkit/Mesh.hh"
 #include "zenkit/Archive.hh"
+#include "zenkit/Error.hh"
 #include "zenkit/Stream.hh"
 
 #include <algorithm>
@@ -160,6 +161,14 @@
 					    auto normal_b = c->read_vec3();
 					    std::uint32_t texture_index = c->read_uint();
 
+					    // `texture_index` is read off the file and indexes a vector sized by a
+					    // count read off the file earlier in the same chunk. Nothing ties the
+					    // two together, so an out-of-range index here copy-constructs a
+					    // `shared_ptr` out of whatever is past the allocation.
+					    if (texture_index >= lightmap_textures.size()) {
+						    throw ParserError {"Mesh", "shared lightmap texture index out of range"};
+					    }
+
 					    this->lightmaps.emplace_back(
 					        LightMap {lightmap_textures[texture_index], {normal_a, normal_b}, origin});
 				    }
